{
  "id": "two-city-scheduling",
  "questionId": "two-city-scheduling",
  "slug": "two-city-scheduling",
  "title": "Two City Scheduling",
  "difficulty": "Medium",
  "category": "Greedy",
  "patterns": [
    "greedy",
    "sorting"
  ],
  "lists": [],
  "hints": [
    "start by imagining everyone goes to city B - what does it cost, and how would sending someone to A instead change the total?",
    "sending person i to A instead of B changes the total cost by costs[i][0] - costs[i][1] - some people have a very negative swing (A is much cheaper), others a very positive one",
    "sort people by that difference (costA - costB) ascending - the people at the front save the most by switching to A",
    "send the n people with the smallest difference to city A, and the remaining n to city B",
    "why is this provably optimal? any other valid split can be transformed into this one via a sequence of swaps that each individually reduce or keep equal the total cost, since swapping a higher-difference A-assignee with a lower-difference B-assignee never increases the sum"
  ],
  "commonMistakes": [
    "sorting by raw cost to city A (or city B) alone instead of by the difference between the two costs",
    "sending the n cheapest-for-A people to A without checking whether that leaves the remaining people especially expensive for B",
    "assigning based on whichever city is cheaper for that individual person, without enforcing the constraint that exactly half must go to each city"
  ],
  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "A company is flying 2n people to interviews, and exactly n must go to city A while the other n go to city B. You're given `costs`, where the cost of flying person i to city A is `costs[i][0]` and to city B is `costs[i][1]`.\n\n**Return the minimum total cost to fly everyone so that exactly n people end up in each city.**\n",
    "constraints": [
      "2 <= costs.length <= 100",
      "costs.length is even",
      "1 <= costs[i][0], costs[i][1] <= 1000"
    ],
    "notes": [
      "only 2 people total (n = 1)",
      "everyone has identical costs for both cities",
      "a person for whom city A is far cheaper alongside a person for whom city B is far cheaper"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "Arguments passed into solution function",
    "outputFormat": "Return output matching method signature",
